                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Snow Fortress is a really fun game that honestly took me by surprise. I figured this would be 5 minutes before I got bored but it ended up pulling me in for 2 hours of ducking, dodging, and throwing. Being early access it doesn't currently have a lot of content so I'll be excited to see more levels and items added throughout the process. Right now there are 2 modes, Survival and Snow Fort.\n\nIn Snow Fort you are trying to complete each level by defeating the snowmen behind pre built forts, as levels go up towards twelve they get more difficult by giving the snowmen better bases and vantage points. This was the meat of the game for me, the levels quickly became challenging as you have to think how to build your own fort and where to attack first. Currently I've completed 11/12 levels.\n\nIn Survival you build a base and then face wave after wave of snowmen that aren't behind any cover, as the wave number gets higher you'll begin facing more snowmen. The cool thing about Survival is that it has a global leaderboard.\n\nPros\nCute atmosphere and fox\n12 levels with more to come\nConstant 90fps\nDodging snowballs works great, never got hit when I felt like I shouldn't have.\nLeaderboards in Survival\n\nCons\nFew items although they plan to add more\nVery quiet game, could use some more music\n\nOverall I enjoyed the game a lot and certainly recommend it, judging by the trailer I assumed this would be a very easy game meant just for kids but the difficulty went up nicely and I bet newer levels will be even more challenging. If you want to see some gameplay I also have a video here. https://youtu.be/-Ak4Lim77QU",
